WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
The recording is only part of the story
A video shows what happened. Chapters and recorded notes make the important moments easier to find.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Keep the context beside the work
The video and its metadata live in the same GitHub body. There is no separate service to keep in sync.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Mark useful changes of context
A chapter starts at a timestamp in seconds. Select any chapter to move the video directly to it.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Seeking works in both directions
Jumping backward restores the earlier chapter and notes. Nothing depends on watching from the beginning.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Notes are not a transcript
Record concise observations, decisions, actions, and results. They provide context that the audio may not contain.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Leave room to read
Turn off Follow playback to browse the notes at your own pace. Turn it back on to return to the current moment.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Link to the moment under discussion
Share includes the GitHub source, the selected video, and an optional start time. It never includes an access token.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Ready for another set of eyes
Anyone with access to the source can open the link and explore the same chapters and notes in their browser.
